WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:12.240
You're standing in a street in a&nbsp;
British town in the late Victorian era,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:18.880
the old Queen is still on the throne. It's&nbsp;
a time between the old world and the new.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:31.440
It's a winter's night - cold and moonless.&nbsp;
You should also imagine one more thing -&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:37.360
there's electric street light, high off the&nbsp;
ground the lamp is flickering and hissing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.520
Underneath the street light stands a woman.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:47.600
She has an intelligent, determined face and&nbsp;
curly hair pinned in a mound on top of her head.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:56.000
She's staring up at the electric light - it's an&nbsp;
arc lamp, a wisp of lightning crackling between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.880
two electrodes. She's listening to the hiss,&nbsp;
noticing that when the ark buzzes, the light dims.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:12.480
She knows those lights throw off sparks, they&nbsp;
can start fires. She's imagining a future where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.480 --> 00:01:20.800
electric light could be bright, even and safe.&nbsp;
She's thinking: "How can I make that happen?"

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:27.120
Hertha Marks Ayrton had&nbsp;
always had to be ingenious.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:34.000
Born into a Jewish family in Portsmouth in 1854,&nbsp;
her father was dead by the time she was seven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:40.720
leaving the family with little more than a pile&nbsp;
of debt but Hertha Marks Ayrton&nbsp;was what 

00:01:40.720 --> 00:01:47.520
you might&nbsp;call a bright spark and always inventive.&nbsp;
She was stubborn, tomboyish and outspoken.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:54.480
Every evening for a year after a full&nbsp;
day of work Marks Ayrton studied for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.480 --> 00:02:01.600
the Cambridge University entrance exam. She passed&nbsp;
in 1874 with honours in mathematics and English.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.800 --> 00:02:09.280
She was an astonishingly hard worker and made&nbsp;
her first recorded invention - a sphygmomanometer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:16.640
that would draw a graph of a person's pulse. After&nbsp;
graduating she carried on teaching and inventing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:22.800
In 1888 she delivered a series of six hugely&nbsp;
popular public lectures on electricity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:28.560
in which she held out to her audience a&nbsp;
compelling vision of an electrified future.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:35.840
Electric arc lights were used in street lamps, they&nbsp;
provided incredibly bright lightning in a bottle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:44.000
but they were volatile and poorly understood.&nbsp;
To make them safe and reliable,

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:50.960
someone needed to invent a way to precisely control&nbsp;
their dangerous temperamental power so Hertha Marks Ayrton

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:58.480
asked herself: why did arc lights&nbsp;
flicker and how could she stop them doing it?&nbsp;

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:06.320
She put together an intricate and comprehensive&nbsp;
set of experiments to test out every possibility.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:12.800
She often had to hold the arc steady by hand&nbsp;
for four or five hours to get consistent results&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:20.080
and Marks Ayrton deduced the electric&nbsp;
arc hissed when oxygen was present&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:26.720
in small craters in the carbon surface. The&nbsp;hiss was the sound of the carbon oxidising.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:33.440
To stop this happening, Hertha Marks Ayrton
invented and patented a new kind of carbon rod&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:41.520
coated with a copper film to stop oxygen reaching&nbsp;
the sides of the electrodes. As she predicted this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:49.040
gave a steadier arc a more dependable light.&nbsp;
Marks Ayrton wanted to make street lights safer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:56.960
and she did. The arc light helped create&nbsp;
a new after dark world of working, playing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:05.360
shopping and exploring. She ended up sparking life&nbsp;
into detonators, 3d printing and maybe one day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:13.040
rocket launchers for space travel. Hertha Marks Ayrton tamed lightning - the ark that burned so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.040 --> 00:04:19.360
brightly between the electrodes of those early&nbsp;
lights was uncontrollable. A wisp of lightning,&nbsp;

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:27.840
if you like. Marks Ayrton got that lightning&nbsp;
under her control and gave it to the world.

